## 🔴 Legal Blocker — Must Resolve Before Go-To-Market

> **The metadata-based routing rules engine described in this requirement must not be shipped without a written legal and regulatory position from EMIS Health's regulatory and legal teams on the following question:**
>
> *When EMIS ships a configurable document routing rules engine (no default rules; all clinical logic entered by the practice), does EMIS bear any manufacturer responsibility under UK Medical Devices Regulations 2002 (as amended) for routing decisions made by practice-configured rules?*
>
> **Current analysis (⚠️ Confidence: MEDIUM — not a substitute for formal legal advice):**
>
> EMIS's position is likely defensible provided:
> 1. EMIS ships the rules engine with **no default routing rules** — no clinical logic is pre-configured by EMIS
> 2. EMIS does not claim or market this capability as a clinical routing tool (see Go-To-Market Constraint below)
> 3. EMIS surfaces an in-product disclaimer at the point of rule creation (see Acceptance Criteria — Disclaimer)
> 4. EMIS does not conduct or claim to have conducted a clinical safety assessment of any practice-configured rule
>
> Under this analysis, **the practice** bears responsibility for any rules it configures, potentially as an in-house manufacturer under the own-use exemption (UK MDR 2002). The own-use exemption may reduce (but does not eliminate) the practice's regulatory obligations provided they do not place the configured rules on the market.
>
> **Explicitly out of scope — these scenarios are not supported by the product and must not be enabled:**
> - A practice selling or licensing its configured rule set to another practice
> - EMIS shipping pre-built recommended routing rule templates for common document types
>
> These exclusions are enforced by product design and must be reflected in the customer contract and terms of use.
>
> **Resolution required by:** Before go-to-market. This is a go-live blocker.
> **Owner:** EMIS Head of Regulatory + General Counsel
> **Action:** Obtain written legal opinion. Update this requirement with outcome before V1c design phase.

