## Go-To-Market Constraint

> **This constraint applies to all marketing, sales, product copy, help documentation, and in-product messaging for the routing rules feature.**
>
> The routing rules capability must be positioned and described exclusively as an **administrative efficiency tool** — reducing the manual effort of triaging and routing documents to the appropriate person or team.
>
> The following framings are **prohibited** in any customer-facing material:
> - ❌ "Automatically routes clinical documents to the right clinician"
> - ❌ "Intelligently directs documents based on clinical content"
> - ❌ "Clinical decision support for document triage"
> - ❌ Any framing that implies the product makes clinical routing decisions
>
> Permitted framings:
> - ✅ "Reduce administrative triage time by setting rules that pre-assign documents to the right team"
> - ✅ "Configure routing rules based on document type, source, and urgency to streamline your document management workflow"
> - ✅ "Administrative routing rules — you define the logic, your team saves the time"
>
> This constraint must be reviewed by EMIS Marketing and Legal before any go-to-market materials are published. Breach of this constraint could undermine EMIS's regulatory position on manufacturer responsibility.

