## User Story

As a practice administrator,
I need to create tasks linked to inbound documents and either assign them manually or have them routed automatically by rules I have configured based on document metadata,
So that clinical and administrative work arising from documents reaches the right person quickly without requiring manual triage of every document.

**Acceptance Criteria:**

### Task Creation (manual)
- [ ] A task can be created from any document in the inbox. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Each task has: **Task Type** (required; sourced from EMIS Web user task types), due date, priority (Urgent / Routine / Administrative), assignee (individual or role-group), and free-text instructions. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Multiple tasks can be created simultaneously from a single document, each routed independently. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] For NHSmail-source documents, Document Manager task creation follows the same queue flow as other sources: ingest first, match in Document Manager (REQ-011), then create filing/coding/tasks in Documents workflow. NHSmail service task records are not authoritative for Document Manager queue decisions. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] A document cannot be marked as fully done until all associated tasks are completed. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The task trail (task creation, completion) is visible on the document. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The **Assign to** selector in task creation uses the current EMIS-X user picker as its source of assignable users/role-groups. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The tasking panel must not display the warning text "Completing this document will update the corresponding EMIS". *(Must Have)*

**Task Type values source:**
Task Type values are sourced from the EMIS Web user task type configuration at runtime; a hardcoded fixed list is not used in this release.

### Task Queue List View
- [ ] The Task Queue lists all open tasks assigned to the current user or their role-group(s). *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Each row in the Task Queue displays the following columns in order: Urgency, Document Title, Patient, Assigned To, **Task Type**, **Created** (date the task was created), Due, Actions. The Urgency column displays a red arrow indicator for Urgent documents; non-urgent documents display no indicator. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The Tasks list can be **filtered by the Assigned To field**. When an Assigned To filter is active, it is displayed as a removable tag above the document list. The filter can be cleared by removing the tag. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Selecting a row navigates the user directly to the associated document in the document viewer. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Tasks in the Task Queue can be completed in any order, regardless of the sequence in which they were created or assigned. The order of task completion is at the user's discretion. *(Must Have)*

### Routing Rules (metadata-based)
- [ ] A practice administrator can create, edit, and delete routing rules. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] A routing rule consists of one or more AND conditions evaluated against document metadata fields only: document type, urgency, source, department, and document title (exact string match). *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Rules are evaluated in priority order; the first matching rule fires; subsequent rules are not evaluated. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] A configurable fallback rule applies when no rule matches (default: route to Administrators). *(Must Have)*
- [ ] When no metadata is available on an inbound document, no rule is evaluated and the document is placed in the unmatched/manual triage queue. This is an accepted constraint of the rules engine. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Rule evaluation never reads or analyses document body content. *(Must Have — SaMD boundary enforcement)*
- [ ] Rule evaluation never uses AI, machine learning, NLP, or semantic similarity. *(Must Have — SaMD boundary enforcement)*

### In-Product Disclaimer — Rule Creation
- [ ] A disclaimer is surfaced to the user **before** they save any new or edited routing rule. The user must explicitly acknowledge the disclaimer before the rule is saved. *(Must Have — regulatory)*
- [ ] The disclaimer text states, in substance: *"Routing rules you configure here may constitute a medical device under UK Medical Devices Regulations 2002 (as amended). By saving this rule, your organisation accepts responsibility for the clinical appropriateness of this routing rule. EMIS Health is not responsible for routing decisions made by rules configured by your organisation. This tool is intended to support administrative efficiency in document management."*
- [ ] Disclaimer acknowledgement is recorded in the audit trail (user ERN, timestamp, rule ID). *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The disclaimer is re-surfaced if an existing rule is materially edited (condition change or assignee change). *(Must Have)*

### Out of Scope — Explicitly Prohibited
- [ ] EMIS must not ship default routing rule templates. The rules engine must be empty on first use. *(Hard constraint)*
- [ ] The product must not enable a practice to export, share, or sell its routing rule configuration to another practice. *(Hard constraint)*

