## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — task creation, routing rule firing, disclaimer acknowledgement, and task completion events all audited
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — task trail must be visible on the document to evidence that required actions were taken
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — routing failures must be explicit; a task that fails to reach its assignee must never appear as successfully delivered

### SaMD Boundary Enforcement
The following constraints are non-negotiable and enforce the SaMD boundary. Any future change to these constraints requires a formal regulatory assessment before implementation:
- Rules evaluate document metadata fields only (type, urgency, source, department, title string-match)
- Document body content is never read by the rules engine
- No AI, ML, NLP, or semantic similarity is used at any point in rule evaluation
- EMIS ships no default rules — all routing logic is practice-authored

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-028:** Task not received by intended assignee — clinical action not taken because routing failed silently
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-029:** Multiple tasks created from one document but one is missed — partial action taken; clinical context incomplete
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-031:** Document marked done while outstanding tasks remain — incomplete clinical actions missed
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-032:** Routing rule fires on document with no metadata — document silently misdirected or lost
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium (some inbound sources supply incomplete metadata)
  - **Risk Level:** High
  - **Mitigation:** No rule fires when metadata is absent; document placed in manual triage queue (accepted constraint)

- **HAZ-DOC-033:** Practice configures a routing rule that constitutes a medical device without understanding the regulatory implications
  - **Severity:** Medium (regulatory/liability risk rather than direct patient harm)
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** High
  - **Mitigation:** In-product disclaimer with mandatory acknowledgement before rule is saved; audit trail of acknowledgement; go-to-market framing constraint

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-027:** Task routing failure surfaces explicit error to task creator; failed delivery never shown as successful
- **MIT-DOC-028:** Document cannot be marked fully done while any associated task remains incomplete
- **MIT-DOC-031:** No rule evaluated when document metadata is absent; document placed in manual triage queue
- **MIT-DOC-032:** Mandatory disclaimer acknowledged before rule saved; acknowledgement audited

