## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance

### KPIs
- Task creation rate (per document, per practice)
- Routing rule hit rate (% of documents matched by a rule vs. falling through to fallback)
- Routing rule fallback rate (% of documents reaching fallback — high rate indicates rules need tuning)
- No-metadata rate (% of documents with insufficient metadata for rule evaluation — operational signal for source quality)
- Task completion time (task created → task marked complete)
- Disclaimer acknowledgement rate (% of rule saves where disclaimer was acknowledged — monitoring compliance)

### OTEL Spans
- `documents.task.created` — task created; assignee type (individual / role-group) recorded
- `documents.task.routed` — task successfully delivered to assignee queue
- `documents.task.routing_failed` — task failed to reach assignee; error type recorded
- `documents.task.completed` — task marked complete by assignee
- `documents.task.document_done` — all tasks on a document completed; document marked fully done
- `documents.routing_rule.evaluated` — rule evaluation triggered; match result (matched/fallback/no-metadata) recorded; rule ID if matched
- `documents.routing_rule.created` — new routing rule saved; disclaimer acknowledged flag recorded
- `documents.routing_rule.amended` — existing routing rule edited; disclaimer re-acknowledged flag recorded
- `documents.routing_rule.disclaimer_acknowledged` — user explicitly acknowledged disclaimer; rule ID, user ERN, timestamp

### SLOs
- Task routing: p95 < 2 seconds from task creation to appearance in assignee's task queue
- Rule evaluation: p99 < 200ms (deterministic lookup; no AI inference)
- Task creation: p95 < 1 second

