## PxD (Added by V1d)

> **Scope: Full PxD.** UI surfaces: Task step in document workflow (Step 4 of StepIndicator), Tasks tab queue list, Routing Rules admin screen, Rule Builder screen, routing disclaimer modal. Shared components from REQ-001 (StepIndicator, Protocol Panel, Queue-Peek Sidebar) reused — not re-specified here.

---

### User Flow

**Primary Flow — Create a task during document workflow (Step 4):**
1. Admin completes Steps 1–3 (Match → File → Code); StepIndicator advances to Step 4 "Task"
2. Protocol Panel shows Task form: AI-suggested task type (confirmed or overridable), description, assignee (from EMIS-X user picker), urgency, due date
3. `Banner variant="warning"` shown: EMIS Web workflow state write-back warning (models are not equivalent)
4. Admin clicks "Complete document ✓" — task created; document moves to Completed tab; `Notification variant="success"`
5. Skip option: Admin can click "Skip task →" to complete without creating a task (if permitted by practice policy)

**Primary Flow — Work from Tasks queue tab:**
1. Admin clicks "Tasks" tab — Tasks queue list shows: Matched Patient, Urgency, Document Title, Task Title, Assigned Person
2. Admin filters by "Assigned to" (own tasks / all tasks / specific user)
3. Admin opens a task → document viewer opens; Protocol Panel shows task details
4. Admin marks task complete → `Notification variant="success"` + audit event; task removed from Tasks tab

**Primary Flow — Configure a routing rule (Practice Admin):**
1. Admin navigates to Settings → Routing Rules
2. Admin sees `Banner variant="warning"` with SaMD / legal disclaimer (persistent — not dismissible)
3. Admin clicks "+ Create rule" — Rule Builder screen opens
4. Admin enters: rule name, conditions (AND logic; metadata only), assignee (from user picker), task type (from EMIS Web task types), priority order
5. Admin clicks "Save rule" — routing disclaimer `Dialog` opens; admin must acknowledge before save commits
6. Rule appears in priority-ordered list; fallback shown (Routes to Administrators)
7. Audit event recorded (CLIN-002)

**Exit Types:**
- Task step: "Skip task" (no task created, document completed) / "Complete document" (task created, document completed)
- Rule builder: Cancel returns to Routing Rules list; no rule created
- Routing disclaimer: Cancel = rule not saved; rule builder remains open

